<article class="env-lemma" id="0DJG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DJG">Lemma <span data-tag="0DJG">15.85.8</span>.</a> Let $R' \to A'$ be a flat ring map of finite presentation. Let $R' \to R$ be a surjective ring map whose kernel is a nilpotent ideal. Set $A = A' \otimes _{R'} R$. Let $K' \in D(A')$ and set $K = K' \otimes _{A'}^\mathbf {L} A$ in $D(A)$. If $K$ is $R$-perfect, then $K'$ is $R'$-perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Observe that $A' \to A$ has nilpotent kernel and that by flatness of $R' \to A'$ we have $K = K' \otimes _{R'}^\mathbf {L} R$ (see Section <a href="/tag/065Y" data-tag="065Y">15.62</a>). Hence the lemma follows by combining Lemmas <a href="/tag/0H76" data-tag="0H76">15.77.4</a> and <a href="/tag/0H75" data-tag="0H75">15.68.20</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>